  "notes": "3D-printed replacement for a goBILDA 1141 90° bracket, same footprint and plate-side screw holes. Print in PETG or nylon (not PLA), 5 walls, 40% gyroid, lying on its side (a gusset face on the bed) so the layers run around the corner. The open holes in the two gussets let them flex instead of cracking when the robot takes a hit; the slot in the top leg lines up with any channel hole pattern. M4 screws + nylon locknuts."
